# Keep the build context small and the image clean. Without this, `fly deploy`
# uploads .venv and .git (hundreds of MB) on every deploy, and secrets in .env
# would be baked into the image layer.

# Secrets — never bake these in. Both hosts inject config as env vars/secrets.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local virtualenv — the image installs its own dependencies.
.venv/
venv/
env/

# VCS + tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Python build noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Runtime data. Excluded per-subdirectory rather than as a whole `database/`, because
# Docker cannot re-include a path whose parent directory is excluded — a blanket
# `database/` would silently drop database/learning_data/userdata.txt, which the FAISS
# memory index is built from, with no error at build time.
database/chats_data/
database/vector_store/
database/camera_captures/
database/quizzes/
database/tts_cache/
# Live state belongs in S3, not baked into an image layer where a deploy would
# resurrect a stale copy over newer data. Listed individually rather than as
# `database/*.json` so it is obvious what is dropped, and so nothing nested
# (database/uploads/records.json) is caught by accident.
database/lectures.json
database/schools.json
database/division_progress.json
database/division_doubts.json

# Logs and local scratch
*.log
_server_*.log
_commitmsg.txt
_maharaja_analysis/
system-role.zip

# Docs and tests aren't needed at runtime
docs/
tests/
*.md
!README.md
